deep.reconstruction:
There is no mathematics on this page. Folio 140v carries no independent writing. What is visible is faint brown ink in the right half of the leaf, and it is show-through (bleed-through) from the other side of the same leaf, the page given as the 'previous page' (140r). The faint text matches 140r line for line:
- the opening two lines 'Mit jedem einfachen Denkact tritt etwas Bleibendes, Substantielles, in un- / sere Seele ein.';
- the paragraph 'Dieses Substantielle ... ich nenne es daher „Geistesmasse“';
- the one line that reaches far to the left, which is the long inserted parenthesis '(die Verschiedenheit des Processes, in welchem sie sich bilden)';
- the struck-out words near the 'Ihr Eintreten in die Seele' paragraph;
- the indented paragraph 'Die Seele ist also eine compacte ... Geistesmasse';
- the numbered theses 4), 5) and 6);
- the closing parenthetical remark about Denken and Kraftaufwand.
The content is Riemann's psychological-metaphysical fragment on 'Geistesmassen' (mental masses): their formation, their permanent connections, and their need for a material carrier only while they are being formed. It is philosophy of mind and Naturphilosophie, with no formulas, derivations or computations. On the verso itself there is nothing to reconstruct.
